From: Ziyang Huang <hzyitc@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: allow four-byte QPIC NAND identification

QPIC transports READID through one 32-bit NAND_READ_ID register. Compare
at most the three device bytes available after the manufacturer byte.
This lets the ESMT entry match before falling through to a shorter
GigaDevice entry with different geometry.

SPI-only extraction of qualcommax/0411-mtd-qpic-four-byte-nand-id.patch;
the raw NAND hunk is deliberately excluded. This target-local workaround
relaxes SPI NAND comparisons throughout the qualcommbe kernel, not only
for QPIC. Recheck prefix collisions when updating the device tables.
No ECC parameters or chip geometry definitions are changed.

Original-commit: cf5225a6e279995a574a5ed97cb227b5e076ed8e
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Signed-off-by: Ziyang Huang <hzyitc@outlook.com>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
@@ -1409,7 +1409,7 @@ int spinand_match_and_init(struct spinan
 		if (rdid_method != info->devid.method)
 			continue;
 
-		if (memcmp(id + 1, info->devid.id, info->devid.len))
+		if (memcmp(id + 1, info->devid.id, min(3, info->devid.len)))
 			continue;
 
 		nand->memorg = table[i].memorg;
